{{--
    The navigation icon sprite.

    Every Lucide symbol (0.544) the icon map can produce, each referenced once per link as
    <svg class="nav-icon"><use href="#i-name"></use></svg>. One copy of
    the geometry per page instead of one per link, and one place to fix
    an icon rather than fifty-five.

    WHY A SPRITE AND NOT INLINE PATHS

    Inline would put ~15KB of path data into every nav render, repeated
    for the desktop rail and again for the mobile drawer, and changing
    one icon would mean finding every copy of it. The sprite is emitted
    once by the layout and the links carry a four-word reference.

    WHY THE STROKE ATTRIBUTES ARE IN CSS AND NOT HERE

    <use> clones a symbol into a shadow tree whose inherited context is
    the <use> element, NOT this sprite -- so presentation attributes put
    on the <svg> below would never reach the cloned paths. They live on
    .nav-icon instead, which is the element doing the referencing.

    These paths are Lucide's own, taken from the published package
    rather than retyped: every id below maps from the Font Awesome name
    it replaced through NavIcons::MAP, and a test asserts that every
    `use href` on a rendered page resolves to a symbol defined here.
--}}
